-- title:
--   Unfolding an adelic Epstein integral along the rational mirabolic subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix a character $\omega\colon(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times}\to\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ of the units of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ all of whose values have absolute value $1$, real numbers $a,b$, and a set $\Phi_0$ of adelic points of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ satisfying `IsSlabDomain a b Φ₀`, i.e. $0<a<b$ and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$ under `globalPointsGL` with respect to the slab measure `slabMeasure a b`; fix also a finite, non-zero measure $du$ on the group of unit finite ideles (those units $\delta$ of the finite adele ring with $\delta$ and $\delta^{-1}$ integral at every height-one prime), with the measurable structure pulled back from the Borel structure on the adeles along $u\mapsto$ `finUnitIdele u`. Let $P$ be the intersection of the subgroup generated by those adelic matrices whose row of index $2$ equals $(0,0,1)$ with the range of `globalPointsGL`. Then there exist $c$ with $0<c<\infty$ in $\mathbb{R}_{\ge0}^{\infty}$ and a set $\Omega$ that is a fundamental domain for $P$ with respect to the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` on adelic $\mathrm{GL}_3$ such that for every $F$ in `cuspFunctions ω a b Φ₀` (a member of `automorphicSubmodule ω a b Φ₀` that is continuous and is cuspidal along $P_{21}$ and along $P_{12}$ for the pin datum `productionPinsOf ℚ ∅ (fun _ => ⊥) (fun _ => 1) (AdelicBox.adelicBox ℚ)`), every measurable $\Phi\colon\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{3}\to\mathbb{C}$ and every real $\sigma$, the lower integral of $\|F g\|^{2}\cdot$ `AdelicEpstein.epsteinPlus du Φ σ g` against `domainMeasure a b Φ₀` (the slab measure restricted to $\Phi_0$) equals $c$ times the lower integral over $\Omega$, against `adelicGLHaar`, of $\|F g\|^{2}\,\|\Phi(e_3 g)\|\,\bigl(\|\det g\|^{\sigma}\bigr)$, where $e_3 g$ denotes the row of index $2$ of $g$ and $\|\det g\|$ is the idele norm `TateGlobal.ideleNorm` of $\det g$.
--
--   This is the unfolding step of the Rankin–Selberg integral of the square of a cuspidal automorphic function on $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ against the diagonal adelic Epstein–Eisenstein sum `epsteinPlus`: the sum over non-zero rational vectors $\xi$ collapses, up to a finite positive constant, to a single integral over a fundamental domain for the rational mirabolic group. It feeds the subsequent identification of the slab integral with a multiple of a quotient-measure integral.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_isFundamentalDomain_mirabolic_and_lintegral_domainMeasure_eq_mul_lintegral.lean

